      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T15:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can run checkpatch on your patch instead of the file. I use this git hook in my global .gitconfig to avoid having to manually create patch files:\n```\n[alias]\n        checkpatch \u003d !sh -c \\\"git rev-list \\\\${*:-@\\\\{upstream\\\\}..HEAD} | xargs -L 1 sh -c \u0027git log --format\u003d\\\\\\\"%n%n%h %s%n\\\\\\\" \\\\$1^..\\\\$1 \u0026\u0026 git show --format\u003d\\\\\\\"From: %aN \u003c%aE\u003e%n%s%n%n%b\\\\\\\" \\\\$1 | scripts/checkpatch.pl --max-line-length\u003d80 --strict --ignore\u003dGERRIT_CHANGE_ID -\u0027 - | less -FXSR\\\" -\n```",
      "parentUuid": "86356579_48a0d3bb",
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
