        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T01:58:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like I happened to draw inspiration from drivers that use a for-loop instead of \"for_each_sg\". I\u0027ll change it.",
      "parentUuid": "c6f967fc_4a608177",
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "130fbdf2_05f664d8",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T15:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure you can use that to create the sg list. There are helper functions to create the sg list from other kernel data structures which is want I was asking for, but I don\u0027t see a common one for this. Other drivers create their own static one, e.g. external/linux/drivers/media/v4l2-core/videobuf-dma-sg.c",
      "parentUuid": "10c6cd1e_c769508a",
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
