      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T15:54:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I thought you were just objecting to the loop itself, since you asked about \"a helper function for this loop\".",
      "parentUuid": "130fbdf2_05f664d8",
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc4cdff3_8d43efa6",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-14T23:33:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "_compat was only used to support old trusty versions that expects a pure physical address as the argument to SMC_SC_SHARED_LOG_ADD. Unless your vmalloc allocation happens to be contiguous trusty_share_memory_compat/trusty_share_memory will fail for those trusty version anyway. Should we just add a early version check in this probe function as well?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "290b59aa_c775c5fc",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T01:58:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And if that added version check fails, do you want to fail this probe function, or fall back to the old code that uses alloc_pages?\nIf the intent is to fail, I\u0027m not convinced it\u0027s worth adding another version check here just so we can fail a little sooner.",
      "parentUuid": "bc4cdff3_8d43efa6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b12effe9_999f10f1",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T15:39:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to drop the _compat suffix, you should to add a version check or you could accidentally pass a bad value to an old trusty version. The current code is OK, as it could accidentally work with an old trusty version. I think this could use a comment though.",
      "parentUuid": "290b59aa_c775c5fc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bfdcf41_f14ac624",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T15:54:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The _compat function calls trusty_transfer_memory, which has a version check already. Is that not sufficient?",
      "parentUuid": "b12effe9_999f10f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c021ded_ef5ca1e2",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T16:30:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That version check is only if the number of entries in the list is more than 1. In the current version of your code that seems to always happen though, so yes, that is technically sufficient as longs as you don\u0027t change anything (e.g. TRUSTY_LOG_NUM_PAGES). sg_alloc_table_from_pages which trusty-test.c calls into merge adjacent pages though so if your code is updated to have the same behavior, then _compat is needed to handle the case where nents is 1 and we call into an old trusty version.",
      "parentUuid": "9bfdcf41_f14ac624",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ec4110509f5b84f5976e3b03ca3cbf0afdd2b13a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
